      "writtenOn": "2023-10-05T17:00:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In a normal cable, if there are both TBT and DP mode VDOs, they should match in their capabilities. But you could imagine a defective cable that advertised, for instance, retimer in the TBT VDO but redriver in the DP VDO.\n\nIn that case, it\u0027s not obvious to me what the TCPM should do, but it seems like the behavior should at least be self-consistent, i.e. if we relied on the TBT VDO to decide that we could enter DP mode, then we should be entering TBT mode on the cable and configuring the retimer based on the TBT VDO.\n\nIt seems like the structure of this code would allow for us to configure retimer/redriver based on the TBT VDO but configure optical based on the DP VDO. That seems like an opportunity to be subtly wrong. (This same reasoning may also apply to the general mode entry logic in the DP module.)\n\nDo you think this is a legitimate concern?",
      "revId": "4785cd32b2da59a461f82d101e6d0534dd7be961",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4eea4790_672fbaef",
        "filename": "driver/retimer/bb_retimer.c",
        "patchSetId": 71
      },
      "lineNbr": 326,
      "author": {
        "id": 1427817
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-05T17:09:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure this is a legitimate concern cause in that case wouldn\u0027t the cable be violating the spec? I added these additional checks in the case the cable doesn\u0027t support dp mode vdos but does support tbt mode vdos.\n\nretimer_handle_dp21_dfp is only called when we are in mux state dp enabled so we know we are in DP mode not TBT mode. There exists a small (but non zero) chance that the device is DP 2.1 but someone used a cable that only supports TBT VDOs.",
      "parentUuid": "c9d19fc4_aef7faea",
      "revId": "4785cd32b2da59a461f82d101e6d0534dd7be961",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
